### 4. HTML Rendering (context-view.ts, lines 1426–1457)

This is the complete rendering pipeline for the Recommendations tab:

```typescript
let recommendationsContent = "";
if (data.synthesisTopActions.length > 0) {
  const escHtml = (s: string): string =>
    s.replace(/&/g, "&amp;").replace(/</g, "&lt;").replace(/>/g, "&gt;").replace(/"/g, "&quot;");

  const viewDetails = data.synthesisReportPath
    ? ` <a class="view-details-link" data-report-path="${escHtml(data.synthesisReportPath)}">View Details</a>`
    : "";

  const actionItems = data.synthesisTopActions
    .map((a) => {
      const tagsHtml = a.tags.length > 0
        ? " " + a.tags.map((t) => `<span class="tag-pill tag-${t}">${escHtml(t)}</span>`).join("")
        : "";
      return `<li>${escHtml(a.action)}${tagsHtml}</li>`;
    })
    .join("\n        ");

  const remaining = data.synthesisTotalActions - data.synthesisTopActions.length;
  const moreLabel = remaining > 0
    ? `<div class="more-actions">+${remaining} more recommendation${remaining === 1 ? "" : "s"}</div>`
    : "";

  recommendationsContent = `
    <div class="tab-header-row">
      <span class="tab-section-label">Recommendations (${data.synthesisTotalActions})</span>
      ${viewDetails}
    </div>
    <ol class="actions-list">
      ${actionItems}
    </ol>
    ${moreLabel}`;
} else {
  recommendationsContent = `<div class="muted">No recommendations available</div>`;
}
```

Tags are fully rendered as inline `<span>` elements appended after the action text in each `<li>`.

---

### 5. CSS Styling for Tags (lines 1953–1968)

```css
.tag-pill {
  display: inline-block;
  font-size: 10px;
  line-height: 1;
  padding: 2px 6px;
  margin-left: 4px;
  border-radius: 9px;
  vertical-align: middle;
  opacity: 0.85;
  background: var(--vscode-badge-background);
  color: var(--vscode-badge-foreground);
}
.tag-coverage    { background: var(--vscode-charts-blue, #3794ff);   color: #fff; }
.tag-congruency  { background: var(--vscode-charts-purple, #b180d7); color: #fff; }
.tag-completeness{ background: var(--vscode-charts-orange, #cca700); color: #fff; }
.tag-impact      { background: var(--vscode-charts-red, #f14c4c);    color: #fff; }
```

The CSS uses a **convention of `tag-{value}`** where the tag value from the JSON (e.g., `"coverage"`, `"congruency"`, `"completeness"`, `"impact"`) maps directly to a CSS class via `tag-${t}`. Four specific tag values have dedicated color overrides. Any other tag value falls back to the default VS Code badge colors.

---

### Summary

Tags **are fully implemented** in the rendering pipeline, end-to-end:

| Stage | What happens |
|---|---|
| `findQualitySynthesisData()` | Finds `quality-synthesis-data-v*.json` on disk |
| `loadSynthesisActions()` | Parses `prioritized_actions[].tags` (string array) from JSON, passes top 5 |
| `ContextData.synthesisTopActions` | Types tags as `string[]` per action |
| HTML render (line 1438) | Emits `<span class="tag-pill tag-{value}">{value}</span>` per tag |
| CSS (line 1953–1968) | Base `.tag-pill` style + 4 named color classes: `coverage`, `congruency`, `completeness`, `impact` |

The tab itself is added to the panel whenever `synthesisTopActions.length > 0` OR `hasProjectAppgraph` is true (line 1516), ensuring the "Recommendations" tab is always present once a project appgraph exists.

